# MCP-First Pattern

**MCPs are your FIRST resort, not your last.**

Before reaching for Grep, Read, WebSearch, or manual exploration:
1. STOP
2. Check the routing table below
3. If a task matches an MCP domain, USE THAT MCP
4. If no match, proceed with file-based tools

## MCP Routing Table

| Domain | MCP Server | Triggers |
|--------|------------|----------|
| github | `pr-workflow` | PR, pull request, PR comment, review comment, resolve thread, CI status, CI failure, code scanning, CodeQL, security alerts, github |
| coverage | `codecov` | coverage, codecov, test coverage, patch coverage |
| qstash | `qstash` | qstash, workflow runs, workflow logs, dlq, dead letter queue, failed workflow |
| project-management | `linear-extra-utils` | upload plan to linear, push plan to ticket, update ticket description |
| observability | `dash0` | logs, traces, production logs, debug production, observability |
| database | `mongodb` | database, mongodb, query, find documents, check entity |
| research | `perplexity` | search, research, find out, what is, how to, latest, best practices |
| web-scraping | `firecrawl-mcp` | scrape, crawl, read URL, fetch page |
| deployment | `vercel` | vercel logs, build logs, runtime logs, deployment status |
| documentation | `context7` | docs, documentation, API reference, library docs, how to use |
| research | `exa` | search, code examples, research, deep search |
| errors | `sentry` | error, sentry, stack trace, exception, crash |
| development | `next-devtools` | next.js, dev server, routes, server errors |
| documentation | `notion` | notion, ERP docs, API documentation, meeting notes |
| code-intelligence | `serena` | find symbol, find function, find class, where is, who calls, references to, go to definition, refactor, rename |
| customer-support | `pylon` | pylon, customer support, customer issue, support ticket, customer account |
| project-management | `linear` | ticket, linear, issue, create ticket |
| github-platform | `github` | GitHub Actions, workflow runs, job logs, list commits, search code, list branches, get file contents, list releases, who am I, GitHub user, GitHub team, team members, approve PR, request changes, PR review, submit review, update PR, update PR branch |
| aws-observability | `aws-cloudwatch` | cloudwatch, aws logs, cloudwatch logs, cloudwatch metrics, cloudwatch alarms, log insights, aws monitoring |

## Prohibited Patterns

1. Using Grep to find functions/classes when `serena` is available
2. Using `WebSearch` when `perplexity` or `exa` exists
3. Using `gh` CLI via Shell when `pr-workflow` MCP exists
4. Making up documentation instead of fetching it (use `context7`)
